("series.art.20261108", "prompt", "Create a richly illustrated editorial cover for an article series for teenagers, Growing Up in the Way of Jesus. No words, no lettering, no logos. Warm detailed painterly realism, like an illustrated storybook for older readers, luminous Australian coastal golden-hour light, amber timber and eucalyptus greens, textured brushwork with convincing natural details, sophisticated and inviting. At a modest timber verandah on a coastal hillside, two older teenagers about 16 to 17 are quietly making and discovering things together: one seated at a wooden worktable with a small open sketchbook and a half-finished wooden boat, another near the verandah rail looking out toward a winding garden path and the expansive turquoise ocean. They wear normal contemporary casual clothes and have natural relaxed poses. A couple of ordinary books, a shell and a mug on the table; no legible markings. Native flowers and eucalyptus frame the scene, small honey-coloured house on the left, sunlight through leaves, welcoming open horizon on right, visual sense of curiosity, friendship and room for a future. Make the central human scene legible when a wide landscape image is cropped to a nearly square hero. Landscape 1536x1024 composition. Do not depict Jesus, parents or small children, no halos, crosses, charts or motivational symbols, no fantasy buildings, no staged worship pose. These are imagined fictional people, not portraits.")
